1. Project Title
Auto Ticket Classification using Flow Designer
2. Introduction
The Auto Ticket Classification using Flow Designer project is an automation solution developed for a school IT helpdesk.
The system classifies IT support tickets based on the issue described in the Short Description. The solution uses ServiceNow Flow Designer to automate ticket classification and email notification.
3. Problem Statement
The school IT helpdesk receives multiple incident requests from students and teachers, such as Wi-Fi issues, projector failures, password problems, and slow computers.
IT staff manually review each request and assign the appropriate category and subcategory. This process is time-consuming and inefficient.
4. Objectives
Automatically classify incidents at the time of creation.
Reduce manual effort for IT agents.
Improve ticket routing efficiency.
Implement a no-code and easily maintainable solution.
Send automated email notifications to callers.
5. Proposed System
The proposed system uses ServiceNow Flow Designer to analyze keywords in the Short Description of a newly created ticket.
Based on the identified issue, the system assigns the appropriate Category and Subcategory.
The system also sends an automated email notification to the Caller after ticket creation.
6. System Components
ServiceNow Platform
Incident WorkFlow table
Project Update Set
Category and Subcategory fields
Flow Designer
Email Notification
7. Category and Subcategory Classification
Category
Subcategory
Network
Wi-Fi
Hardware
Projector
Access
Forgot Password
Performance
Slow Computer
The Subcategory field is configured as a dependent field based on Category.
8. Automation Process
The Flow Designer automation is triggered when a new record is created and the Category field is empty.
The flow checks the Short Description and classifies the ticket.
Wi-Fi / Network → Network → Wi-Fi
Projector / Hardware → Hardware → Projector
Password / Login → Access → Forgot Password
Slow / Hanging → Performance → Slow Computer
9. Email Notification
After classification, an automated email is sent to the Caller.
Subject:
Your Request for the issue has been submitted.
The email provides confirmation that the support request has been submitted.
10. Testing and Validation
The system was tested using different IT support scenarios.
Test Case 1 – Wi-Fi Issue
Short Description:
WiFi not working in library
Result:
Category: Network
Subcategory: Wi-Fi
Email notification sent to Caller
Test Case 2 – Projector Issue
Short Description:
Projector not turning on.
Result:
Category: Hardware
Subcategory: Projector
Email notification sent to Caller
11. Project Outcome
The project provides an automated ticket classification system for a school IT helpdesk.
The solution reduces manual classification effort, provides consistent Category and Subcategory values, and improves communication through automated email notifications.
12. Conclusion
The Auto Ticket Classification using Flow Designer project provides a complete automation solution for school IT helpdesk ticket classification.
The solution uses ServiceNow Flow Designer to classify IT tickets based on the Short Description. Dependent choice fields help maintain accurate data, while automated email notifications provide confirmation to the Caller.
The project uses a no-code approach, making the solution easy to maintain and scalable for small to medium environments such as educational institutions.
